	<article id="post-122274" class="post-single post-122274 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-beauty category-skincare tag-experiment-beauty mustard">
		<header class="entry-header">
			<ul class="entry-meta type-3">
				<li class="entry-date">8.26.25</li>
				<li class="post-category"><a href="https://thestripe.com/category/beauty/" title="View all posts in beauty" >beauty</a></li>			</ul><!-- .entry-meta -->

			<h1 class="entry-title">Experiment Beauty Review</h1>
					</header><!-- .entry-header -->

		<div class="entry-content">
			<input class="jpibfi" type="hidden">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img data-perfmatters-preload fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1535" src="https://thestripe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Experiment-Beauty-Review-1024x1535.jpg" alt="Experiment Beauty Review" class="wp-image-122275" title="Experiment Beauty Review" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt="The skincare brand you need to know, especially if you have dry skin. They just launched at Sephora, most of their products are $30 or under, and the products are highly effective and hydrating. " data-jpibfi-post-url="https://thestripe.com/experiment-beauty-review/" data-jpibfi-post-title="Experiment Beauty Review" data-jpibfi-src="https://thestripe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Experiment-Beauty-Review-1024x1535.jpg" srcset="https://thestripe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Experiment-Beauty-Review-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://thestripe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Experiment-Beauty-Review-475x712.jpg 475w, https://thestripe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Experiment-Beauty-Review-200x300.jpg 200w, https://thestripe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Experiment-Beauty-Review-768x1151.jpg 768w, https://thestripe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Experiment-Beauty-Review-1366x2048.jpg 1366w, https://thestripe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Experiment-Beauty-Review.jpg 1500w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This sounds silly, but I feel like I am maybe just a little bit clairvoyant when it comes to moisturizer. Really now, I wish I could apply this possible clairvoyance to another area of my life, but it seems like moisturizer is the one area where I can predict what&#8217;s going to be big. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Why do you ask? I was one of the first to fall in love with <a href="https://thestripe.com/dr-augustinus-bader-the-cream-review/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Augustinus Bader</a> when it launched (before it was even at Violet Grey). And then INN Beauty&#8217;s Rich Cream. The next big thing? Experiment Beauty. You have to try this brand! In June, I wrote on Substack that we&#8217;d be seeing them everywhere soon, and boom: looky look, <a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23783967" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">they&#8217;ve just launched at Sephora</a>. This brand is excellent, especially for those of you with dry skin. And the products are . . . highly inexpensive for what they are.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">Experiment beauty review</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So far, I&#8217;ve tried three products (and really like them all). Here are my thoughts!</p>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading"><a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23784318" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Plasma Wash</a></h5>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is an ultra-creamy face wash that almost feels bouncy? It&#8217;s super soothing, and the consistency <em>feels</em> really good. The only other cleanser I have to compare it to is <a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23784110" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">U Beauty&#8217;s Mantle cleanser</a>. If you gave them to me to try blind, I don&#8217;t think I would be able to tell them apart. And the best part? This one is a quarter of the price. Highly recommend if you are looking for a gentle, creamy cleanser that takes off all your makeup without stripping the skin. <strong>Get it on the <a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23784318" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">brand&#8217;s website</a> or at <a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23784915" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Sephora</a></strong>.</p>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading"><a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23785162" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Super Saturated</a></h5>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is the brand&#8217;s signature item, and it is fabulous. Any time my skin feels parched, I&#8217;ll apply this under my moisturizer, and it is like it brings my skin back to life. This is thanks to Polyglutamic Acid and 30% glycerin. It is not an anti-aging serum, but it is one of the best hydrators I&#8217;ve tried. Makes skin so plump and dewy. You can also use it like a mask. Also: $28! And they sell refills! <strong>Get it on the <a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23785162" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">brand&#8217;s website</a> or at <a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23785251" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Sephora</a></strong></p>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading"><a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23785424" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Molecular Mesh</a></h5>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is a great basic moisturizer aimed at restoring the skin&#8217;s barrier. Again, it does not have any fancy anti-aging ingredients like Bader or U Beauty <em>but</em> it will hydrate just as well as those moisturizers. I would compare it to <a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23785572" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Rhode&#8217;s Barrier Restore Cream</a>, which is a very similar price. <strong>Get it on the <a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23785424" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">brand&#8217;s website</a> or at <a href="https://go.shopmy.us/p-23839757" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Sephora</a></strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Disclosure: If you buy something through my links, I may earn an affiliate commission at no cost to you. I only feature things I truly love here. Thanks for your support</em>.</p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->

		
		<footer class="entry-footer flex">

			<div class="entry-photographer type-3"><p>Photography by Laura Saur.</p>
</div>
			<div class="comments-link type-3"><a href="#comments">Let's get to the comments</a></div>

		</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
	</article><!-- #post-122274 -->

			
			<div class="pubexchange_module" id="pubexchange_below_content" data-pubexchange-module-id="3428"></div>

			
